        <item>
            <title>1.7.0</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:09:16 +0200</pubDate>
            <link>https://miq.marco-duering.net/</link>
            <sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>https://github.com/marcoduering/MIQ/releases</sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>
            <sparkle:version>1.7.0</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.7.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description>&lt;style&gt;
body { line-height: 1.45; margin: 10px 12px; }
h1, h2, h3 { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; margin: 14px 0 4px; }
h1:first-child, h2:first-child, h3:first-child, p:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
p { margin: 0 0 8px; }
ul, ol { margin: 0 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; }
li { margin: 2px 0; }
code {
  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  font-size: 0.92em; background: rgba(128,128,128,.14);
  border-radius: 3px; padding: 1px 4px;
}
&lt;/style&gt;
&lt;p dir="auto"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul dir="auto"&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Files on external drives (SSD or HDD, APFS or exFAT) are now memory-mapped instead of being read in full before the preview appears. 4D files open &lt;strong&gt;up to 14× faster&lt;/strong&gt;, and memory use stays low even for files of several hundred MB.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Faster first preview of large files: MIQ now tells macOS in advance which parts of a file the preview needs, so they're read in large chunks instead of small pieces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p dir="auto"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul dir="auto"&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thumbnails: a &lt;strong&gt;Skip large (compressed) files&lt;/strong&gt; setting controls the size limit above which compressed MGH, MIF and NRRD files keep Finder's standard icon (default 100 MB).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/marcoduering/MIQ/releases/download/v1.7.0/MIQ.app.zip" length="4640035" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="DxI2UTW5fRy7cvESqCHuAUqg5OIQJ1+aUEGHssAJZ5LtTtlWTNqhMSs52tSXaXsJR1FO0LZhxS7sUa99E5pKBQ==" />
